      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Domenici is praising President Bush's gasoline price plan and discussing what Congress must do. He is not claiming personal responsibility for any concrete policy outcome, which represents position-taking and general policy discussion rather than credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1862",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "This press release matches Positive Example 1. Senators Baucus and Tester explicitly claim credit for delivering on their promise to secure $12.5 million in federal funding for vital military projects in Butte, Montana."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "871",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Salazar is questioning and criticizing the Secretary of the Interior over budget cuts. This is an oversight activity without a completed, successful deliverable, which is excluded from credit-claiming according to the negative clarification."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2675",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The senators are lobbying BRAC commissioners to keep Sub Base New London open. They note that 'until we reach the finish line... our work isn't done,' meaning there is no finished, successful outcome yet. This represents ongoing advocacy/promising to fight rather than credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3744",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Inouye announces that he was 'informed' by the CDC about plans to establish a field station in Hawaii. Although he mentions a past facility created at his request, he does not claim personal responsibility or active agency in securing this new forward base, representing a general announcement."
